## Policy

To describe the procedure to be followed by applicable agency personnel in any incident where Life Saving Victoria is involved.

## Procedure

### 1. Purpose of incident notifications

Certain roles are required to be notified of incidents as they occur to ensure strong incident coordination, effective incident management and appropriate oversight of the incident. These notifications also support any member well-being response that is required during or after an incident.

The roles required to be notified vary with the nature of the incident, its characteristics, its outcome, its location and the units involved. Under the LIMSOC Incident Categorisation model these are recorded as the Incident Type, Tags, Incident Outcome, Agency Status, Area and responding units. Notification rules in this SOP are expressed against those fields.

### 2. The incident subscription list

Every incident in LIMSOC carries a subscription list. The subscription list is the set of roles and units that receive notifications for that incident and is the recipient set for all incident paging under this SOP.

A role or unit is added to the subscription list when any trigger configured for it (section 3) is present on the incident. Where more than one trigger applies to the same role, the role is subscribed once. Triggers are evaluated when the incident is opened and again whenever the incident changes: when the Incident Type is refined or corrected, a Tag is added, the Agency Status changes, a unit is attached, a condition is met, the Incident Outcome is set, or the LSV Comms Supervisor adds a subscriber.

Every member of the subscription list receives every notifiable event for the incident. There is one subscription list and one feed for each incident. The notifiable events are:

1. Incident opened
2. Incident Type refined or corrected
3. Tag added
4. Agency Status changed
5. Unit attached or released
6. Protracted condition met
7. Incident Outcome set
8. Incident closed
9. Broadcast by the LSV Comms Supervisor to the subscription list

A role or unit added to the subscription list after the incident is opened receives, as its first notification, a summary of the incident as it stands.

Any role or unit on the subscription list may be cleared at any time by LSV Comms. A cleared role or unit receives no further notifications for that incident unless re-added. Clearing is recorded in the incident chronology with the time and the operator. Clearing does not alter the incident's Type, Tags, Status or Outcome.

### 3. Notification triggers

A trigger is a fact about an incident that, when present, subscribes one or more roles to that incident. Triggers are of seven kinds.

| Kind | Source | Evaluated |
|---|---|---|
| Type | The Incident Type node. A rule on a node applies to every descendant unless marked node-only. A child may add roles; a child never removes roles inherited from its parent. | At open, at refinement, at correction |
| Tag | A controlled Tag on the incident | When the Tag is added |
| Outcome | The Incident Outcome. The Outcome is set as soon as it is known and is required at closure. | When the Outcome is set |
| Condition | Protracted: 60 minutes have elapsed since the Agency Status was first set to Responding without the Agency Status reaching Under Control. Evaluated by LIMSOC and fires once. | When the condition is met |
| Area | The incident is located in an Area Response Officer's Area, or a unit from that Area is attached to the incident. Where the incident Area cannot be resolved, the Vic-wide fallback applies. | At open and whenever a unit is attached |
| Derived | State resource tasked: one or more state-level assets (helicopter, RWC, ERU, RPAS, state vehicle) attached as a responding unit. Multiple services responding: two or more lifesaving services attached as responding units. | Whenever responding units change |
| Manual | The LSV Comms Supervisor adds any role or unit to any incident at any time. Recorded in the incident chronology. | When taken |

An incident opened at a Not Final Type subscribes the roles on that node at open. Refinement to a child Type adds the child's roles. Correction of a miscategorised Type adds the roles of the corrected Type; roles subscribed under the incorrect Type remain subscribed unless cleared.

