### 5. Attendance

Attendance expectations are separate from notification. The subscription list determines who is informed; this section determines who is expected to attend or to consider attending.

| Trigger | Should attend | Consider attendance |
|---|---|---|
| Outcome: Fatality | ARO | |
| Tag: Resuscitation | | ARO |
| Tag: Member Injury | | ARO |
| Tag: Media Interest | | SAC, SMO |

The State Duty Officer attends at their discretion or at the direction of the State Agency Commander.

### 6. Method and recording

Notifications are issued electronically through LIMSOC to the subscription list. Where the circumstances require it, LSV Comms provides a verbal briefing in addition. The time and method of every notification, every addition to the subscription list, every clearing and every broadcast are recorded in the LIMSOC incident chronology. Individuals monitoring an incident directly are to create an incident message stating that they are monitoring in the Incident Log.

## Activity Logs

Members will need to record activity in the appropriate LSV logs. Refer to SOP 4.4 – Activity Logs for additional requirements.

## Special Considerations

All members need to ensure that the protection and preservation of life is always maintained. In the application of this SOP, the following safety considerations apply:

- All members are responsible for identifying hazards, monitoring and assessing risk. Any incident which involves an injury, near miss, damage to equipment or any other hazard observed in the workplace should be reported as soon as practicable.
- The safety of the individual member and others should always be considered.

