## Annex B – LIMSOC platform requirements

1. Type rules inherit down the Incident Type tree; a node may be marked node-only.
2. Rules may be configured on Tags, Incident Outcome, a Protracted timer (minutes since Responding without Under Control), Area of incident, Area of attached unit, state resource tasked, and count of responding services.
3. A per-incident subscription list, persisted with the incident, computed as the union of all rules that have fired plus additions by the LSV Comms Supervisor.
4. Every notifiable event (Procedure section 2) is sent to the whole subscription list; a newly added subscriber receives an incident summary first.
5. Any subscriber may be cleared at any time by LSV Comms, with the clearing recorded in the chronology.
6. All notifications sent, and all subscription changes, are recorded in the incident chronology with time, method and operator.
7. Rules and recipients are configurable in the administrative portal without redevelopment.
8. Incident Outcome may be set at any time once known and is required at closure.
9. Tags required: Media Interest (new), and Needle Stick, Spinal, Fracture, Dislocation, Attack Reported, Major First Aid, Mass Rescue, Off-duty response, Resuscitation, Member Injury, Extrication as in the Incident Labels taxonomy.

